\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Ends Higher In Spot Mkt As Dlr Slips Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht perked up against the dollar in spot trading Monday, buoyed by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline against the Japanese yen and the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums dropped amid brisk dollar-selling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'Funds are coming in, and the baht is more stable,' a dealer at the Bank of America said. 'Traders feel more confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Monday, the dollar was at 25.945 baht, down from 25.962 baht at the close of trading Friday. That indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars at below-market rates from Thai commercial banks, since the dollar finished outside the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.95 to 25.99 baht Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's midrate for the dollar was 25.97 baht Monday, unchanged from Friday. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, the mark and the yen. It tends to rise whenever the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls against the yen and the mark. At the close of trading in Bangkok Monday, the dollar was at 123.40 yen, down from 123.45 yen in New York late Friday. The dollar was at 1.6878 marks, down from 1.6950 marks in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates, meanwhile, declined amid the dollar-selling. The overnight and call interbank rates closed at 9.5%, down from 10% to 10.5% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1109GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3h01u13\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
