\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Ends Lower In Spot Mkt As Dlr Gains Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht slipped against the U.S. dollar in spot trading Monday, hurt by the dollar's rise against the Japanese yen late Friday - which drove the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band higher. \par \par \uc2  But the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums declined amid dollar-buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Monday, the dollar was at 25.940 in the spot market, up from 25.932 baht at the close of trading Friday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, set its mid-rate for the dollar at 25.95 baht, up from 25.93 baht Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's level indicated no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened and closed within the the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band Thursday was 25.93 baht to 25.97 baht. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar's rise against the yen late Friday caused the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the band from 25.91 to 25.95 on Friday. The dollar closed at 121.90 yen in New York Friday, up from 121.13 yen on Thursday. Around 1042 GMT (5:42 a.m. EST), the dollar was 121.83 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the decline in swap rates to growing investor confidence in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite worries about the health of the country's financial system. Moody's Investors Service has threatened to downgrade Thailand's long-term debt ratings, and Thai finance companies suffered runs of more than $1 billion last week. \par \par \uc2  'Sentiment in the baht is getting better because investors think the government is doing something about the problem (among finance companies),' a dealer at a U.S. bank said. As for Moody's, he said, have 'already factored in the possibility that Moody's will downgrade long-term debt.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1105GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3a01p4e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
