\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Down In Early Trading Amid More Dlr-Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 04:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is down in early spot trading Monday, hurt by a continuing sell-off following the decision by Moody's Investors Service Friday to review the country's long-term debt rating for a possible downgrade. \par \par \uc2  But the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mixed in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell baht at specified times in the future. One-month premiums declined although all other premiums increased. \par \par \uc2  Around 0231 GMT (9:31 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading at 26.095 baht, up from 26.035 baht at the close of trading Friday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed the mid-rate for the dollar at 25.99 baht, the highest rate since April 26, 1990. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the baht's slump to dollar-buying by investors nervous about Moody's decision to review Thailand's A2 long-term debt rating for possible downgrade. 'There's still bad sentiment,' a dealer at the Bank of America said. 'People are still selling baht.' \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by mid-morning Monday, although the dollar is currently trading near the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range of 25.97 baht to 26.01 baht. \par \par \uc2  The dollar-buying has driven up interbank rates. The overnight interbank rate and the call rate are both at 22%-25%, up from 20% Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates are as follows, in satang (1 baht equals 100 satang):\par        Monday      Friday      Thursday     