\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Baht -2: Baht-Selling Tightens Market Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1997\par 04:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Reports of the default, which broke out hours before Somprasong filed a confirmation to the Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET), also helped drag the stock market down 2.7% Wednesday. The SET index closed at 744.50 points Wednesday, down 20.83 points from a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  Many investors are also selling the baht in favor of the dollar as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to rise against the Japanese yen, dealers said. Around 0346 GMT (10:46 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 123.58 yen, up from 123.32 yen late in New York Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many commercial banks are also experiencing liquidity crunch, resulting from a selloff in baht and increasing demand for cash during the Chinese New Year. Meanwhile, the Friday deadline for mandatory reserve requirements, during which banks are required to deposit 7.0% of their funds with the Bank of Thailand, is also helping to dry up excess money supply in the interbank market. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rates are being quoted in a wide range between 18.0%-20.0%, the highest level since Jan. 13, 1995, compared with 20.0% late Wednesday. The call rate is unquoted at 0315 GMT (10:15 p.m. EST) but was 15% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  No \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reported, but some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not want to inject cash into the system while the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still on a hot streak for fears that interbank players will spend much of the money they borrowed from the bank on accumulating the advancing dollar. \par \par \uc2  'I haven't seen any indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market,' said a dealer at a leading Thai bank. 'But that may be because they don't want to banks to buy more dollars. That won't be good for the baht.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0350GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2600rrf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
