\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Ends Dn In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkts On Devaluation Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1997\par 12:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht slumped in the spot and swap markets Thursday, hurt by false devaluation rumors that apparently led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened against the dollar in the spot market. Amid heavy dollar-buying, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished at 25.812 baht, up from 25.800 baht Wednesday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, set its mid-rate for the dollar at 25.79 baht, up from 25.75 baht on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumors of an imminent devaluation, first reported by the financial-information service Technical Data late Wednesday, triggered a sell-off in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pushed the dollar to an intraday high of 25.830 baht around 0300 GMT Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand immediately denied the rumors, saying traders may have misunderstood recent comments by its deputy governor, Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi, who warned Thai businesses with U.S-dollar risks to hedge those risks because of the danger of big fluctuations in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  'I think the market was trying to make a big story out of Khun Chaiyawat's comments,' a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. 'He only said people should be aware of the pronounced \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations and take the necessary precautions. That's just a comment to warn exporters who have exposure to the U.S. dollar. It has nothing to do with baht policy.' \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to the rumors by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market in Singapore. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it doesn't confirm or deny \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But a senior bank official, in denying the rumors early Thursday, said the bank was 'watching the market closely.' He then added: 'You know what that means.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1137GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1n00hml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
