\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Ends Dn In Spot Mkt As Dlr Surges Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht slumped in Asian spot trading Wednesday, hurt by the dollar's advance to a 32-month high against the Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  perked up the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums fell as investors sold dollars in favor of baht in the swap market to capitalize on healthy interest-rate differentials. \par \par \uc2  At the close of spot trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 25.688 baht, up from 25.642 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, set its mid-rate for the dollar at 25.69 baht, up from 25.66 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, the yen and the Deutsche mark. Dealers attributed the baht's decline in the spot market to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge against the yen. Around 1044 GMT, the dollar was at 117.38 yen, up from 116.93 yen at the close of trading in New York Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hadn't been above 117.04 yen since March 29, 1994. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates, meanwhile, fell on rumors that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower them. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the repurchase market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment, although the bank's governor, Rerngchai Marakanond, told reporters late Wednesday the bank intends to keep interbank rates below 11%. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate closed at 9.5%, down from 10.5% Tuesday. The call rate was also at 9.5%, down from 10.5% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1055GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1f007ht\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
