\par\par \b \uc2  Thai finmin says Thai baht undervalued. \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Dec 17 (Reuter) - Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Virawan said on Tuesday that the baht was still undervalued contrary to some analysts' views that it was overvalued. \par \par \uc2  "Many analysts say that the baht is not at a level where it is overvalued. Many think instead that it is undervalued," he said while making a policy statement to a gathering of businessmen and bankers at his ministry. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht came under attack by offshore speculators on Monday and Tuesday as it dropped against the rising dollar on active selling, especially in the Singapore market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said demand for dollars from companies for year-end book squaring also pushed the baht down. \par \par \uc2  They said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to defend the baht by selling dollars in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay did not comment directly on the baht attack. But he said he would try to maintain the stability of the baht and ruled out the consideration of any change in the baht fixing policy in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "There would be no consideration of the baht policy right now. We are confident that we will be able to maintain the stability of the baht (under the current system)," he said. \par \par \uc2  After his comments, the baht stabilised somewhat to 25.590-25.595 against the dollar at 0759 GMT after sliding to a low of 25.612 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently fixes the daily value of the baht against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by using a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , heavily weighted in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Minister said the policy of making the baht more flexible would be considered later by relevant agencies when the need arises. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsch026gk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
