\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand says baht defence cost below $500 mln. \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Dec 17 (Reuter) - Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rerngchai Marakanond said his bank on Tuesday spent less than $500 million in market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht in the Singapore market. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai declined to say how much the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) used to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but said: "It was not as much as $500 million...even if I knew, I could not tell you. If it was that much, it would have needed my approval. If it was less than that, officials could do it by themselves." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers had speculated that the BOT spent about $500 million to defend the sliding baht. \par \par \uc2  The governor said he believed market speculation against the baht this week could be attributed to position squaring by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers as the market approached Christmas and the New Year. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht which fell sharply early on Tuesday perked up after two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore, where speculators had launched attacks on the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in addition to the seasonal factors. \par \par \uc2  At 1013 GMT, the baht stabilised to 25.585-25.595 against the dollar after dipping to a day's low of 25.612 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said he would lead senior policy makers in briefing foreign fund managers and market analysts on government economic policies at his ministry on January 6. \par 