\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Falls To 14-Month Low On Grim Economic Data \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1996\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht fell to its lowest level in more than 14 months Friday as investors, nervous about economic data released Thursday, dumped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened in the swap market, where investors agree to buy dollars at a specified time in the future. Swap premiums rose as grim economic news eclipsed other news of banks making long-awaited interest rates. \par \par \uc2  At the close of spot trading, the dollar was at 25.533 baht, up from 25.523 baht Thursday, and the highest level since Sept. 1 1995. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed its midrate for the dollar at 25.51 baht, up from 25.49 baht Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors abandoned the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the release Thursday of economic data showing a 9.3% decline in exports in September. Data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also showed exports growing just 0.9% year-on-year for the first nine months of 1996, compared with 24% for the full year of 1995. \par \par \uc2  'People were thinking: 'The Thai economy looks bad,'' said a dealer with the Bank of Tokyo. 'Foreign banks were doing a lot of dollar-buying.' \par \par \uc2  The sell-off in the baht, he said, prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Singapore. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't announce the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman couldn't be reached for comment. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, did little to stop the sell-off: at the end of trading Friday, the dollar was trading above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's selling price of 25.53 baht. That suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at below-market rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-11-96 \par \par \uc2  1127GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbt019ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
