\par\par \b \uc2  Plans for free floating baht needed now - KTT. \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Nov 20 (Reuter) - Thailand's fixed exchange rate would be inappropriate and probably unsustainable in a more liberalised financial environment, Krungthai Thanakit said its November economic report released on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The finance and securities firm said a fixed baht may be appropriate given current conditions, but preparing to freely float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and planning monetary policies under floating rate conditions must now be a priority. \par \par \uc2  At present the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets the Thai baht's exchange value each day against a basket of international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely weighted to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  if trading threatens to take the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than two satang either side of this set rate. "Now is the time to consider fully not only what should follow the baht basket ... The first-order answer has to be a floating exchange rate," said Krungthai Thanakit. \par \par \uc2  The report said that the fixed baht has caused some policy conflicts, and monetary management this year may have been easier under a freely-floated regime. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary growth in 1996 could have been very much smoother had the BOT (Bank of Thailand) not commiitted to a fixed baht exchange rate," it said. "Once the constraint of a fixed exchange rate has gone, what will the monetary policy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  be, how will it be imposed, and how will it be monitiored?" \par \par \uc2  Recent pressure on the baht, sparked by slowing exports and a large current account deficit, required direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas swap markets for the first time. \par \par \uc2  Krungthai Thanakit's call for plans to float the baht support comments made in Hong Kong yesterday by Narongchai Akrasanee, the chief of General Finance and possible economic advisor to the new Thai government. \par \par \uc2  Narongchai said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be made more flexible following the introduction of Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures and options markets in mid-1997. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsbk004ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
