\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Thailand says baht has normalised. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 16 (Reuter) - Bank of Thailand Governor Rerngchai Marakanonda said the baht had now returned to normal after being under pressure for some time. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai told reporters late on Sunday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Exchange Equalisation Fund (EEF) had bought dollars worth US$902 million between September 1-13. \par \par \uc2  The baht was sold heavily offshore on devaluation rumours between late July and early August and then again in early September, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This forced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through offshore swap markets for the first time to defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai declined to reveal the total amount used in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said the situation was now calm. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand's EEF sold dollars worth about US$770 million in July and a "small amount" in August, he added. \par \par \uc2  "So far, the amount of net capital outflows is not at a worrying level. And we keep monitoring the situation closely," he said. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai also reiterated that the Bank of Thailand had no policy to devalue the baht, something the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said many times to allay fears about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's future. \par \par \uc2  But he declined to comment on whether the Bank of Thailand planned to widen the dollar/baht trading band any time soon to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now allows the baht to trade within a four-satang band, two satang on the down or upside, against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9g033dg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
