\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus/Thailand-3: Fears Of Policy Drift \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1996\par 05:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The most favorable outcome of the two September events, analysts say, would probably be a Fed decision not to raise interest rates in combination with a decision by Banharn to resign - either before or after a no-confidence vote. The least favorable result would be an unscathed Banharn government and a Fed move to boost interest rates. \par \par \uc2  But whatever the outcome, economists say, \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets to keep the baht stable. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than $1.8 billion in such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early August following rumors that it was about to devalue the baht. It has since been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  more or less every week, although the magnitude of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  has diminished. \par \par \uc2  One reason is that investors may worry, even if Banharn resigns, that Thai economic policy is adrift at a time when the country can't afford it. The U.S. credit-rating agency Moody's Investors Service, for example, last week downgraded the country's short-term sovereign debt to Prime-2 from Prime-1, warning that Thailand's accumulation of short-term debt had exposed it to a 'financial shock.' The Bank of Thailand has said it is taking steps to reduce short-term debt. \par \par \uc2  'To have an election now would be quite dangerous,' said Saker of Crosby. 'There would be a feeling of policy drift until a new government is in place, and that would be bad for economic stability.' Arporn Chewakrengkai, an economist with Deutsche Morgan Grenfell Securities in Bangkok says, 'It would be the end of the year before a new government could come in.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-09-96 \par \par \uc2  0301GMT \par \par \uc2  1192 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds9c07dax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
