\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Up In Late Trading As Dlr Down Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 1996\par 14:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht rose against the dollar in late Asian trading Friday, benefiting from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading, the dollar was quoted at 25.284 baht in the spot market, down from 25.293 baht on Thursday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed the midrate for the dollar at 25.28 baht, down from 25.29 baht Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the baht's advance to the U.S. dollar's drop against the Japanese yen. Around 1025 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 107.72 yen in Tokyo, down from 107.93 yen late in New York Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The interbank rates, meanwhile, dropped as money supply expanded, dealers said. Increasing demand for funds in the interbank market helped push the interbank rates up, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it injected 14 billion baht into the repurchase Thursday to ease interbank rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also called off its weekly bonds auction Friday to help maitain money supply. As a result, the overnight rate dropped to 12% from 14.5% Thursday. The call rate also dropped to 12% from 15% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Repurchase rates also dropped. The 1-day rate was at 10.5%, down from 11% Thursday. The 7-day rate was at 10.375%, down from 10.75% Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates were mostly stable. Swap rates are as follows in satang.\par (100 satang = 1 baht).\par     Friday      Thursday    Wednesday 