\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Dn In Early Trading As Dlr Advances Vs Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1996\par 04:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is down against the dollar in early Asian trading Thursday, hurt by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance against the Japanese yen and the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, that investors have begun selling dollars in the swap market on fears of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official confirmed that the Bank of Thailand was checking rates in the swap markets. \par \par \uc2  'We made checks,' the official said. 'Whether we decide to engage in any transaction is another matter.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at 25.307 baht in the spot market, up from 25.288 baht at the close of trading Wednesday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed its mid-rate for the dollar at 25.29 baht, up from 25.27 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that includes the dollar, the yen and the Deutsche mark. Dealers said the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell partly as a result of the dollar's advance against the yen late Wednesday, which prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its midrate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 108.12 yen in New York Wednesday, up from 107.64 yen the previous day. It closed at 1.4897 marks, up from 1.4760 marks on Tuesday. The dollar has since retreated slightly versus the yen and the mark. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said foreign investors remain nervous about the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of jitters about the stability of the government, which could face a no-confidence motion next week. But amid worries of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors sold dollars in the swap markets. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-08-96 \par \par \uc2  0222GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8f06n1j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
