\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2  Baht Ends Up Amid Big  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  By  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1996\par 13:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht inched up against the dollar in Asian trading Thursday, despite a late-afternoon bout of selling by investors betting on the advancing U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 25.259 baht in the spot market, down from 25.273 baht Wednesday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed its mid-rate at 25.22 baht, down from 25.27 baht Wednesday. The cut in the mid-rate was the deepest in nearly nine months, and was aimed at propping up the baht, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht's climb was aided considerably by big \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against rumors of a possible devaluation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it injected 10 billion baht into the Thai repurchase market and bought an unspecified amount of dollars from spot markets in Singapore and Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had never before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign markets. But because this week's devaluation rumors presented the bank with pressures it hadn't faced since Mexico's peso crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used tactics it developed in response to the Mexico crisis. \par \par \uc2  'We'd rather tackle the problem at its root,' said Paiboon Kittisrikangwan, the chief analyst in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking department, of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore and Hong Kong. Dealers said the devaluation rumors originated in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  As of Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had used as much as $1.5 billion of its reserves to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the interbank market. Interbank rates had risen Wednesday to a 19-month high of 26% as commercial banks scrambled to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-08-96 \par \par \uc2  1149GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8106a6t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
