\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Up In Early Asian Trading Amid Dlr-Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1996\par 05:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht continued to climb against the dollar in early Asian trading Thursday, bolstered by a sell-off in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by commercial banks eager to shore up the domestic money supply. \par \par \uc2  Around 0250 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 25.256 baht in the spot market, down from 25.273 baht at the close of trading Wednesday. The Bank of Thailand, meanwhile, fixed the mid-rate for the dollar at 25.22 baht, down from 25.27 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's decline against the Japanese yen and the Deutsche mark Wednesday prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower the mid-rate. Late in New York Wednesday, the dollar was quoted at 106.83 yen, down from 107.96 yen Wednesday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 1.4725 marks, down from 1.4770 marks. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, the yen and the mark. Because of the peg, the baht tends to rise when the dollar declines against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket. \par \par \uc2  Local commercial banks in need for funds also sold the dollar to shore up money supply in the interbank market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it has pumped 15 billion baht into the repurchase market to ease interbank rates. That effort, some dealers said, did little to help. \par \par \uc2  'The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helpful, but not enough,' said a chief money market dealer at one top-five bank. 'Money circulated in the interbank market can be as high as 40 billion baht a day.' \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate was at 25%, down from 26% Wednesday. The call rate, meanwhile, was at 25%, down from 26% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 31-07-96 \par \par \uc2  0350GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds810697h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
